207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 126 0 R
/T (Build a complete ML-KEM-512 forward and inverse transform on an open PDK, SKY130, that runs a full RTL-GDSII ASIC flow for students, hobbyists, and educators to learn from and edit for their liking)
/E (Build a complete ML-KEM-512 forward and inverse transform on an open PDK, SKY130, that runs a full RTL-GDSII ASIC flow for students, hobbyists, and educators to learn from and edit for their liking)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [80]
>>
endobj
208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 126 0 R
/T (The Algorithm)
/E (The Algorithm)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [81]
>>
endobj
209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 126 0 R
/T (Every ML-KEM-512 polynomial product runs as a forward transform on each operand, 128 small products in the transform domain, then one inverse transform.)
/E (Every ML-KEM-512 polynomial product runs as a forward transform on each operand, 128 small products in the transform domain, then one inverse transform.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [82]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 126 0 R
/T (The transform is three nested loops. The outer loop steps through the 7 layers, halving the stride each time. The middle loop walks the blocks in a layer and draws one new twiddle factor per block. The inner loop issues the butterflies, which are independent inside a layer. )
/E (The transform is three nested loops. The outer loop steps through the 7 layers, halving the stride each time. The middle loop walks the blocks in a layer and draws one new twiddle factor per block. The inner loop issues the butterflies, which are independent inside a layer. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [83]
>>
endobj
211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 126 0 R
/T (All 128 twiddle factors sit in a table on the die, so the host sends an index and never a constant.)
/E (All 128 twiddle factors sit in a table on the die, so the host sends an index and never a constant.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [84]
>>
endobj
212 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 126 0 R
/T (The Datapath)
/E (The Datapath)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [85]
>>
endobj
213 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 126 0 R
/T (The chip is the modular arithmetic engine of the transform. A host holds the 256 coefficients and walks the address pattern, the chip does the arithmetic and looks up its own constants. In total, six operations cover the whole flow, with every one of them taking5 clocks.)
/E (The chip is the modular arithmetic engine of the transform. A host holds the 256 coefficients and walks the address pattern, the chip does the arithmetic and looks up its own constants. In total, six operations cover the whole flow, with every one of them taking5 clocks.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [86]
>>
endobj
214 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 126 0 R
/T (Both reduction kernels are on the die. Montgomery follows every multiply, Barrett runs on the addition path of the inverse transform, where there is no product to absorb the radix factor. The multiplier is pipelined across five stages, with two 16 by 8 partial products in place of one 16 by 16, which is what closed timing without a hard multiplier block.)
/E (Both reduction kernels are on the die. Montgomery follows every multiply, Barrett runs on the addition path of the inverse transform, where there is no product to absorb the radix factor. The multiplier is pipelined across five stages, with two 16 by 8 partial products in place of one 16 by 16, which is what closed timing without a hard multiplier block.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [87]
>>
endobj
