798 0 obj
<<
/Title (The chip is the modular arithmetic engine of the transform. A host holds the 256 coefficients and walks the address pattern, the chip does the arithmetic and looks up its own constants. In total, six operations cover the whole flow, with every one of them taking5 clocks.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 784 0 R
/Next 799 0 R
>>
endobj
799 0 obj
<<
/Title (Both reduction kernels are on the die. Montgomery follows every multiply, Barrett runs on the addition path of the inverse transform, where there is no product to absorb the radix factor. The multiplier is pipelined across five stages, with two 16 by 8 partial products in place of one 16 by 16, which is what closed timing without a hard multiplier block.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 784 0 R
/Prev 798 0 R
>>
endobj
